-- title:
--   Node places of the supersingular component avoid smooth residue discs (q=3)
-- statement:
--   Fixed data. A prime $q$ with $q = 3$ (hypothesis `hq3`); a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$ (`hqM'`); a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$ (hypotheses `hℓ`, `hℓ12`, `hℓM'`, the rigid-level guard for the case $q=3$); a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $q$ in the sense that $q$ is a non-unit of $A$ (`hA`); a finite set $W$ of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa, M')$ over the residue field $\kappa = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' κ`, i.e. the rational places that are affine geometric places and whose value at `jGeomGen` lies in `ssJSet q` (`hW`); an element $s \in W$; the inclusion `hle` of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ into $F := \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M' = \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-base change of the function field of level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ for $H = \mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$; a constant reduction $R_0$ of $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa,M')$, with the coefficientwise compatibility `hR₀`: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose image under the coefficient map of $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, that element lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$; and an element $\pi \in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$ (`hπ`, `hπP`).
--
--   Prolongation data. A field $F_{\mathrm{ss}}$ over $\kappa$; a regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ from $F$ to $F_{\mathrm{ss}}$ (a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ of $F$ contracting to $A$, together with a surjective residue map onto $F_{\mathrm{ss}}$ with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $A \to \kappa$, and such that every nonzero element of $F$ has a nonzero-reducing scalar multiple); a finite set $N$ of places of $F_{\mathrm{ss}}$ over $\kappa$; and families $S_Q \subseteq F$ (subrings), $\varphi_Q : A[T] \to S_Q$, $\chi_{0,Q} : S_Q \to \kappa$ and $D_Q \subseteq \{\text{places of } F \text{ over } \overline{\mathbb{Q}}\}$, indexed by the places $Q$ of $F_{\mathrm{ss}}$.
--
--   Hypotheses on these, named as in the statement. `h0`: $F_{\mathrm{ss}}$ contains an element transcendental over $\kappa$. `h1`: $R$ lies over $s$ through $R_0$, namely for every $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ whose order is nonnegative at every place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ at which $j_q$ (the modular invariant, embedded coefficientwise) has nonnegative order, if the $R_0$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$, then the image of $f$ in $F$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R$-residue is the image in $F_{\mathrm{ss}}$ of the value of $s$ at that $R_0$-residue. `h2`: for every $\zeta \in \mathrm{Idx}\,q$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, the pullback of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ is $R.\mathrm{integers}$. `hcard`: $\#N = q+1$. `hpkg` (the smooth-point packages off $N$; fourteen clauses, summarised here): for every place $Q \notin N$, the ring $S_Q$ contains the image of $A$, the map $\varphi_Q$ is formally smooth and formally unramified and sends constants to the images of elements of $A$, $\chi_{0,Q}$ extends the residue map of $A$ and kills $\varphi_Q(T)$, every $c$ in the maximal ideal of $A$ is hit by a unique $A$-section of $S_Q$ lifting $\chi_{0,Q}$ with $\chi(\varphi_Q(T)) = c$, every element of $S_Q$ is $R$-integral with $R$-residue in the valuation subring of $Q$ reducing to the image of $\chi_{0,Q}$, $\varphi_Q(T)$ has $R$-residue of $Q$-order $1$, the set $D_Q$ consists exactly of the rational places $P$ of $F$ that are $A$-integral on $S_Q$ and for which the points of $S_Q$ of $P$-value of valuation $< 1$ are those killed by $\chi_{0,Q}$, each $A$-section as above corresponds to a unique place in $D_Q$, the valuation subring of a place in $D_Q$ is the set of quotients of elements of $S_Q$, a nonzero element of $F$ of order $0$ at all $P \in D_Q$ is a constant multiple of a unit of $S_Q$, and an $R$-integral element regular on all of $D_Q$ lies in $S_Q$. `hdisj`: for $Q, Q' \notin N$, if some place lies in both $D_Q$ and $D_{Q'}$ then $Q = Q'$. `hcusp`: for $Q \notin N$ and $P \in D_Q$, the order of $j_q$ (viewed in $F$) at $P$ is nonnegative. `heqv`: for every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the level automorphisms $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ ($\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$) preserving $R.\mathrm{integers}$, the induced residue automorphism $R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau$ preserves membership in $N$, and for $Q \notin N$ it carries $D_Q$ to the disc of the translated place, the translation of sets of places being `smulDisc`. `hUniq`: for every $Q \notin N$, any quadruple $(S, \varphi, \chi_0, D)$ satisfying the same fourteen clauses coincides with $(S_Q, \varphi_Q, \chi_{0,Q}, D_Q)$ in the sense that $D = D_Q$, $S = S_Q$, and the two residue characters agree on common elements.
--
--   Node data. For each place $x$ of $F_{\mathrm{ss}}$ a field $F_x$ over $\kappa$, a regular prolongation $R_x$ of $A$ from $F$ to $F_x$, and a place $b_x$ of $F_x$ over $\kappa$; an index type $\Lambda$ with subrings $C'_l \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ contained in $A$ (`hC'A`), each a discrete valuation domain with a chosen element $\varpi'_l$, a base index $l_0$; complete discrete valuation domains $W_l$ with elements $\pi_{W,l}$, exponents $E : \Lambda \to \mathbb{N}$ and $E_0 \in \mathbb{N}$; sets $S(x)$ of places of $F$, subrings $\mathcal{N}(x) \subseteq F$ and $\mathcal{N}_0(x,l) \subseteq F$, the latter local (`hloc`) and Noetherian (`hnoe`), and elements $c_x(x), c_y(x), c_u(x) \in F$.
--
--   `hnodes` is a single long conjunction, summarised here, comprising: the coefficient-ring clauses ($\varpi'_l$ cuts out the elements of $C'_l$ with zero residue in $A$; $C'_{l_0} \subseteq C'_l$ for all $l$; $\varpi'_{l_0} \neq 0$; every element of $A$ is algebraic over $C'_{l_0}$; each $\pi_{W,l}$ is irreducible and $E(l) \geq 1$); the tameness clause that every element of the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ with trivial tame character relative to $\pi$ fixes $\varpi'_{l_0}$; the clause that $\varpi'_{l_0}{}^{E_0} = v \pi^{w}$ in $A$ for some unit $v$ and some $w \geq 1$; then, for each $nd \in N$: rationality of $b_{nd}$, of $nd$ and of every place in $S(nd)$; the description of $\mathcal{N}(nd)$ as the elements integral for $R_{nd}$, for $R$ and at every place of $S(nd)$, with values in $A$ at those places; the crossing relation $c_x(nd)\,c_y(nd) = \varpi'_{l_0}{}^{E_0}\,c_u(nd)$ together with the order conditions ($c_x$ reduces to $0$ under $R_{nd}$ and its $R$-residue has $nd$-order $1$; $c_y$ reduces to $0$ under $R$ and its $R_{nd}$-residue has $b_{nd}$-order $1$); invariance of $S(nd)$, $c_x(nd)$, $c_y(nd)$ under the arithmetic Galois action of tamely trivial inertia elements; the clauses that $\mathcal{N}_0(nd,\cdot)$ generates $F$ as a field of fractions, and over $C'_{l_0}$-coefficients; and, for every $l$, the chain $\mathcal{N}_0(nd,l_0) \subseteq \mathcal{N}_0(nd,l) \subseteq \mathcal{N}(nd)$, the characterisation of $S(nd)$ as the places at which $\mathcal{N}_0(nd,l)$ is regular and non-units have value in the maximal ideal of $A$, the inclusion of $C'_l$ into $\mathcal{N}_0(nd,l)$ and approximation of its elements by such constants modulo non-units, a $C'_l$-linear independence clause, the memberships $c_x(nd), c_y(nd) \in \mathcal{N}_0(nd,l)$ with $c_u(nd)$ a unit there, and the existence of $\sigma : W_l \to$ the adic completion of $\mathcal{N}_0(nd,l)$ and of an isomorphism $\iota$ of that completion with the crossing model $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}(W_l, \pi_{W,l}^{E(l)})$ matching $\sigma(\pi_{W,l})$ with $\varpi'_l$, $\iota \circ \sigma$ with the constants, the constants of $C'_l$ with the image of $\sigma$, and converting $b_{nd}$-orders of $R_{nd}$-residues into $V$-adic expansions and $nd$-orders of $R$-residues into $U$-adic expansions; finally the clauses that the sets $S(nd)$, $nd \in N$, are pairwise disjoint; that at every $P \in S(nd)$ the functions $f$ as in `h1` specialise, after subtraction of a representative $a \in A$ of the value of $s$ at the $R_0$-residue, into the maximal ideal of $A$; that each pair $(\zeta', \gamma)$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ induces a self-map $\tau_N$ of the places of $F_{\mathrm{ss}}$ preserving $N$, transporting the sets $S(\cdot)$ and the prolongations $R_{(\cdot)}$; that the group generated by the level automorphisms preserving $R.\mathrm{integers}$ preserves $N$ and carries $S(nd)$ to $S$ of the translated place; that $R_0$-integral functions are $R_{nd}$-integral; and that for each $nd \in N$ there is a ring map $j$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa,M')$ to $F_{nd}$ compatible with the residues of $R_0$ and $R_{nd}$ and comparing the valuation subring of $s$ with that of $b_{nd}$.
--
--   `hSEP1` (the separating-function hypothesis): for every $x \in N$ and every place $y \notin N$ of $F_{\mathrm{ss}}$ there exists $g \in F$ lying in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and in $\mathcal{N}_0(x,l_0)$ such that $g$ is a non-unit of $\mathcal{N}_0(x,l_0)$, the $R$-residue of $g$ is nonzero and has $y$-order $0$, and $g$ lies in the valuation subring of every rational place $P$ of $F$ at which $j_q$ has nonnegative order.
--
--   Conclusion. For every $x \in N$, every place $Q$ of $F_{\mathrm{ss}}$ over $\kappa$ with $Q \notin N$, and every place $P$ of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $P \in S(x)$, one has $P \notin D_Q$: the set of places attached to a node of the supersingular component is disjoint from the residue disc of every smooth point.
--
--   This is the disjointness step in the analysis of the semistable reduction of the full-level modular curve at a supersingular point in residue characteristic $q = 3$, under a rigid auxiliary level divisible by a prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$: the place-sets $S(x)$ belonging to the $q+1$ nodes meet no residue disc $D_Q$ of a smooth point. It is used in the construction of node annuli and of the covering by node presentations and crossing units at the same level.
